# Data processing agreement

**Under Article 28 of Regulation (EU) 2016/679 (GDPR) — version {{ doc.version }}**

## Parties

- **Controller: {{ dot(rec.name) }}**
  - Address: {{ address(rec) }}.
  - {{ tax(rec) }}.
  - Represented by {{ rec.representative }}.
- **Processor: {{ dot(platform.name) }}**
  - Address: {{ address(platform) }}.
  - {{ tax(platform) }}.
  - Represented by {{ platform.representative }}.

## 1. Subject matter

The Processor operates {{ poss(rec.short) }} digital community platform. This agreement sets
out the terms on which the Processor processes personal data on the Controller's behalf
in doing so. Annex 1 describes the processing. Annex 2 lists the security measures and
Annex 3 the sub-processors.

## 2. Duration

This agreement applies for as long as the Processor operates the platform for the
Controller. It ends when that service ends, subject to clause {{ 11 - skip }}.

## 3. Instructions

The Processor processes the personal data only on the Controller's documented
instructions, including for any transfer outside the European Economic Area. This
agreement and the platform's configuration agreed with the Controller are those
instructions. The only exception is where Union or Member State law requires otherwise;
the Processor then informs the Controller before processing, unless that law prohibits
it.

The Processor informs the Controller immediately if, in its opinion, an instruction
infringes data protection law.

{% if features.dso_data_exchange and titles %}
## 4. The Processor's own processing

{% filter wordwrap(88, break_long_words=False, break_on_hyphens=False) %}
The Processor is a separate, independent controller of the meter readings it receives under a member's consent to {{ titles[:-1] | join(", ") }}{% if titles | length > 1 %} and {% endif %}{{ titles[-1] }} for {{ platform.short }}. That processing is governed by the member meter data sharing agreement and by the consent, not by this agreement. The Processor keeps it technically and organisationally separate from the processing under this agreement.
{% endfilter +%}

{% endif %}
## {{ 5 - skip }}. Confidentiality

The Processor ensures that every person authorised to process the personal data:

- has committed to confidentiality, or is under a statutory obligation of
  confidentiality;
- has access only to what their task requires.

## {{ 6 - skip }}. Security

The Processor implements the technical and organisational measures in Annex 2, and
keeps them appropriate to the risk (Article 32 GDPR). It may replace a measure with one
that is at least as effective, and informs the Controller of material changes.

## {{ 7 - skip }}. Sub-processors

The Controller gives general authorisation for the sub-processors in Annex 3.

**Adding or replacing a sub-processor:**

- The Processor informs the Controller at least 30 days in advance.
- The Controller may object on reasonable data-protection grounds within that period.
- If the objection cannot be resolved, the Controller may end the service without
  penalty.

**Obligations passed on:** the Processor imposes on each sub-processor, by contract,
the same data-protection obligations as in this agreement. It remains fully liable to
the Controller for each sub-processor's performance.

