## {{ 9 - skip }}. Assistance

The Processor assists the Controller, taking into account the nature of the processing:

- **Data subjects' rights:** in responding to requests under Articles 15–22 GDPR. It
  forwards to the Controller, within 5 working days, any request it receives directly,
  and does not answer it itself unless instructed.
- **Other obligations:** in meeting the obligations of Articles 32–36 GDPR, including
  data protection impact assessments and prior consultation.

## {{ 10 - skip }}. Personal data breaches

The Processor notifies the Controller of a personal data breach without undue delay,
and in any case within **24 hours** of becoming aware of it.

**What the notice contains**, as far as known at the time (Article 33(3) GDPR):

- the nature of the breach;
- the categories and approximate numbers of data subjects and records concerned;
- its likely consequences;
- the measures taken or proposed.

Information not yet available follows as soon as it is.

## {{ 11 - skip }}. End of the service

When the service ends, the Processor, at the Controller's choice:

- returns the personal data to the Controller in a common machine-readable format;
- or deletes it.

The Processor then deletes the remaining copies within 60 days, including backups when
they expire. The only exception is where Union or Member State law requires retention.
The Processor confirms the deletion in writing.

## {{ 12 - skip }}. Records, audits and inspections

**Records:** the Processor keeps the record of processing activities required by
Article 30(2) GDPR.

**Information:** it makes available to the Controller the information needed to
demonstrate compliance with this agreement.

**Audits:**

- The Processor allows and contributes to audits by the Controller or an auditor it
  mandates, bound by confidentiality.
- Notice: at least 15 working days, except after a breach.
- Frequency: once a year at most, except after a breach or at an authority's request.

## {{ 13 - skip }}. Liability

Each party is liable as provided by Article 82 GDPR.

## {{ 14 - skip }}. Law and jurisdiction

This agreement is governed by Italian law. The courts of {{ platform.forum.en }} have exclusive
jurisdiction.

## Annex 1 — Description of the processing

| | |
|---|---|
| **Services** | Online membership application{{ ', including the reading of an uploaded bill and identity document by a language model' if features.document_extraction else '' }}; community app (energy overview, forecasts, suggestions, commitments, points, notifications, feedback){{ '; AI assistant' if features.ai_assistant else '' }}; login and account management{{ "; the Controller's dataspace connector and identity" if features.dso_data_exchange else '' }}; community console for the Controller's staff |
| **Nature** | Hosting, storage, computation, display, transmission, backup and deletion |
| **Purposes** | Those set out in the Controller's privacy notice for the platform{{ ' and in its notice on sharing meter readings' if features.dso_data_exchange else '' }}, for the Controller's part |
| **Data subjects** | Applicants and members of the community; the Controller's staff using the console |
| **Categories of data** | Identification and contact data (name, tax code, email, phone, address); supply point (POD) and supply address{{ "; copies of an electricity bill and of an identity document, kept until the member's account is activated, and the data read from them (besides the identification data and supply point above: the municipality and the document's expiry date)" if features.document_extraction else '' }}; declared energy equipment; meter and device energy data and data derived from it (forecasts, suggestions, commitments, points); account and login data; notification preferences and delivery records;{{ ' AI assistant messages and attachments;' if features.ai_assistant else '' }} feedback, including screenshots and technical data; records of acceptances and consents{{ "; the member's dataspace identifier" if features.dso_data_exchange else '' }} |
| **Special categories** | None intended{{ '. Members are asked not to provide any to the assistant' if features.ai_assistant else '' }} |
| **Retention** | As in the Controller's privacy notice for the platform, §6 |

## Annex 2 — Technical and organisational measures

**Access and identity:**

- Single sign-on for every application.
- Access by role, enforced by policy on each service.
- Members see only their own data.
- Staff see only their community.
- Multi-factor authentication for administrative accounts.

**Encryption:**

- In transit: TLS on every external connection.
- At rest: storage encrypted at rest. Identification data in the membership application
  is also encrypted per field{{ ', and uploaded documents are encrypted per file' if features.document_extraction else '' }}.
- Secrets: kept encrypted, never in clear in source control.

**Separation:**

- Each community's data is separated by the community identifier and the access
  policies.
- {{ poss(platform.short) }} own research data is kept in separate stores.

**Logging:**

- Administrative actions in the membership application are recorded in an audit log.
{% if features.dso_data_exchange %}
- Every consent decision and every dataspace disclosure is recorded in the dataspace's
  provenance record.
{% endif %}

**Availability:**

- Database backups within the European Economic Area.
- Restore procedures are tested.

**People:**

- Confidentiality commitments.
- Least-privilege access for the Processor's staff.
- Access is removed when a person leaves.

**Development:**

- Changes are reviewed before deployment.
- Dependencies are kept up to date.

